(- Keep the live Baleshop droplet using localhost:3306/bale_shop until a planned migration ) Tj
T* (window.) Tj
T* (- Use YenkasaCode Agent later to plan the Cloud SQL migration, create read-only/app users, ) Tj
T* (import the dump, validate row counts, and switch the Spring Boot datasource only after ) Tj
T* (successful validation.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (SAFE FUTURE TRACE COMMANDS) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Run on the Baleshop droplet:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (bash) Tj
T* (cd /root/triciabales) Tj
T* (grep -RInE 'spring.datasource|jakarta.persistence.jdbc|jdbc:mysql|MYSQL|DB_|DATABASE' . ) Tj
T* (--exclude-dir=target 2>/dev/null) Tj
T* (ss -lntp | grep 3306 || true) Tj
T* (mysql -u balesuser -p bale_shop) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Inside MySQL:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (sql) Tj
T* (SHOW DATABASES;) Tj
T* (USE bale_shop;) Tj
T* (SHOW TABLES;) Tj
T* (SELECT table_name, table_rows) Tj
T* (FROM information_schema.tables) Tj
T* (WHERE table_schema = 'bale_shop') Tj
T* (ORDER BY table_name;) Tj
T* (SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'bind_address';) Tj
T* (EXIT;) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Schema-only dump from the shell, not from inside the MySQL prompt:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (bash) Tj
T* (mysqldump -u balesuser -p --no-data bale_shop > /tmp/baleshop_schema.sql) Tj
T* (head -n 120 /tmp/baleshop_schema.sql) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (SECURITY NOTES) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- The local Spring datasource password appeared in command output during manual discovery. ) Tj
T* (Rotate the Baleshop MySQL password before treating this environment as production-safe.) Tj
T* (- Prefer creating a dedicated read-only database user for YenkasaCode Agent.) Tj
T* (- Do not store live SQL credentials in repo files.) Tj
ET
